      "hints": [
        "Set $2\\tan^2\\theta = 8 \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm 2$.",
        "Find both solutions in degrees for $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the proven identity to $8$:\n$$2\\tan^2\\theta = 8 \\implies \\tan^2\\theta = 4 \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm 2$$",
        "Solve for both angles within the interval $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\text{From } \\tan\\theta = 2: \\quad \\theta_1 = \\tan^{-1}(2) \\approx 63.4^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{From } \\tan\\theta = -2: \\quad \\theta_2 = 180^\\circ - 63.43^\\circ \\approx 116.6^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 63.4^\\circ, \\quad 116.6^\\circ)$$"
      ],
